; combat.eval - the combat rules the code review fixed (docs/code-review-plan.md
; Phase 0c), one section per claim. tools\CombatTest.py runs this and JUDGES it;
; on its own it only reports. Every section header is `=== <name> ===` and the
; judge reads the readouts between one header and the next, so a section must
; stay self-contained: each opens with `reset` and its own seed.
;
; The starter four wear nothing (Brand only CARRIES his armour), so every one of
; them trains `avoid` on a miss - which is what the wind ward sections lean on.
logecho on

; --- THE WIND WARD: a turned bolt teaches nothing (code-review C11) -----------
; An archer shoots at a party warded four times over. Every bolt that reaches a
; member is turned at the deflect stage, before any dice are rolled, so it is
; neither evaded nor blunted: no `avoid` xp, no DEX creep. The ward's charges
; are the count of bolts it turned.

echo === windward ===
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 22
goto eval_arena
arena open 9 9
heal
tp 14 14
face n
freeze off
effect windward 0 99 60
effect windward 1 99 60
effect windward 2 99 60
effect windward 3 99 60
spawn skel_archer 14 9 south
tally reset
step 10
tally
char 0
char 1
char 2
char 3

; The same volley with no ward: what reaches the party is rolled, and a miss
; teaches its target `avoid`. Without this the section above could pass because
; the archer's bolts never trained anything at all.
echo === windward-control ===
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 22
goto eval_arena
arena open 9 9
heal
tp 14 14
face n
freeze off
spawn skel_archer 14 9 south
tally reset
step 10
tally
char 0
char 1
char 2
char 3

; --- ARMOUR IN A HAND: one hand rule for every defensive sum (code-review C12) --
; `char`'s defense line puts the readers side by side: the class
; (WornArmorClass), the pipeline's soak (PartyTarget::Soak) beside the sheet's
; (DefenseFor), and every resist the pipeline would apply. A cuirass carried in
; a hand (`equip` skips the holdable check, so it lands in the hand slot) must
; leave all of them where they were; worn, it must move all of them.

echo === hand-armor ===
reset
timescale 0
char 0
equip plate_cuirass 0 0
char 0
equip none 0 0
wear plate_cuirass 0
char 0
wear none 0

; --- A PIERCING CRITICAL TEACHES THE PLATE NOTHING (code-review C11) ----------
; The armour lesson reads the soak a blow MET (defense::SoakMet), not the soak
; worn: a critical whose piercing edge went under the plate met none of it. All
; four in plate, a bone swarm beside them. Every blow that lands on a standing
; member in plate teaches heavy armour one lesson's xp - except, with `pierce`,
; a critical. `tally` counts the blows that landed (struck) and the criticals
; that went under (pierced); the judge counts the lessons in the xp. The
; control (no `pierce`) is what one lesson pays. Five minutes, because a
; critical that lands is rare against plate (one in 64 blows at seed 22).

