; --- WHERE A FLIGHT ENDS (code-review C43, C44) --------------------------------
; A flight steps and is tested afterwards, so one that met a wall or a shut door
; stopped INSIDE it, a square nobody stands in. Its end is the last open square
; in front (DungeonWorld::FlightEnd): that is where a burst goes off and where a
; bolt's on-hit catches whoever stands there.
;
; A BURST BOLT THAT BREAKS ON A SHUT DOOR goes off on the caster's side of it.
; Maren's Fire Burst (fire project explode) down the corridor at a fresh wooden
; door, a mummy (fire -1, flammable) standing just beyond it. Before C43 the
; burst went off INSIDE the door, a phantom centre that filled both sides of it.
; A firebolt flies 8 m (3.2 squares), so Maren casts from 12,12, 2.25 squares
; short of the door. The judge reads the TALLY's `wallstops=` / `stoppedin=` to
; know the flight stopped IN the door: one whose reach ran out short of it ends
; in the same square in front, and its burst would spare the mummy under the
; old code too - a pass that tested nothing.

echo === burst-door ===
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 23
goto eval_arena
arena corridor 11
heal
tp 12 12
face e
freeze on
editor place doors wooden_door 15 12
mappage close
spawn mummy 16 12 west up
learn 2 fire
learn 2 project
learn 2 explode
setskill 2 fire 5
monsters
breakables 15 12
tally reset
cast 2 fire project explode
step 4
tally
monsters
breakables 15 12

; The control: the same burst with the door OPEN reaches the mummy, so the
; section above cannot pass by the mummy being out of the burst's reach or its
; readout going unread.

echo === burst-door-open ===
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 23
goto eval_arena
