; --- A BURST BOLT THAT REACHES THE PARTY GOES OFF (code-review C1, C18) -------
; A burst (Hagalaz) bolt that reaches a member's lane is its BLAST: it goes off in
; the party's square, on every member there, and no strike rides with it. It used
; to strike one member as a plain firebolt and be retired with the blast unspent,
; so a skel_magus played as a plain firebolt caster. `bolt firebolt_burst` is the
; magus's own bolt (the spell's MonsterBolt), launched from the square ahead down
; Brand's lane (slot 0); a firebolt flies 8 m, so it reaches the party from there,
; in 10 ticks. The readouts come 0.2 s in: the detonation square's tick has
; landed, the burn it left has barely bitten, and the burst's next tick (0.06 s
; on) is spreading through the squares round the party. The judge demands the
; bolt went off WITHOUT expiring: one that flew past the party and burst on the
; wall behind counts a blast too, with an expiry. This is also the control for
; the three sections after it, which change one thing each.

