; --- A FLARE REACHES WHAT IT CAN WALK TO (code-review C17) ---------------------
; Maren's Firelight flare (Sowilo Hagalaz) in a corridor, a shut wooden door two
; squares east. It reaches 3 walking steps - into open squares only, as a blast
; does - so it dazzles and scorches the mummy behind the party (11,12) and the one
; at 9,12, 3 open steps west, and kindles the doused wall torch at 10,12 (2
; steps). The 3-step mummy is what makes the door below mean anything: a reach
; of 2 would keep the mummy beyond it out with no door at all. The corridor ends
; at 9,12, so the square west of it (8,12) is carved open for a fourth mummy, 4
; open steps off, which the flare does NOT reach - so the reach is 3, not more.
; It touches nothing else:
;   - the mummy at 15,12, 3 steps away THROUGH the door, which the old reach map
;     (it walked floor, and a shut door is floor) dazzled and the scorch struck;
;   - the mummy at 18,12, dazzled by hand beforehand: the old scorch struck every
;     monster still dazzled from an earlier flare, wherever it stood;
;   - a wall torch in a lone square carved two north of the party (12,10), behind
;     the rock, which the old kindling reached by Manhattan distance.
; Mummies (fire -1, flammable), so a scorch cannot hide in a resist. `castsvc
; fire` reads each torch from its own square, before the flare and after.

