; --- A PUNCH IS A PUNCH, WHATEVER THE HAND HOLDS (code-review C39) --------------
; Punch and Kick are the bare hand's attacks - the hand menu's Combat group for a
; hand whose item offers nothing of its own, a key or a tablet: an item with no
; `skill`. Both, and the key's own swing, used to take the HELD item's skill,
; which for a key is "", so the blow trained nothing at all. Now they swing, and
; train, unarmed. Brand takes an iron key in his bare left hand (hand 0), a sturdy
; skeleton ahead: four punches, then four of the key's own (neutral) swings. Every
; blow that lands trains `unarmed` by one xp, so the xp gained is the hits counted.
; `char` also names the skill each hand PARRIES with: the key's hand, unarmed.
; Then four punches with his DAGGER hand (hand 1): a punch is the bare hand's
; whatever it holds, so they train `unarmed` too and `blade` not at all. The key
; alone cannot tell that apart from "a key is no weapon" - a key's hand is bare
; under either rule; the dagger's is not.

