; --- A SAVE MADE MID-THROW SETS NOTHING OFF (code-review C47) ------------------
; Brand throws a fire flask and the game is saved while it is still in the
; party's own square, 0.05 s out of his hand. A save used to LAND every thrown
; thing first, and a flask landed is a flask going off: it burst in the party's
; square, the party was hurt, and the save held the damage. Now the save writes
; the flask as the floor item it would be if it came down now, in the square it
; is over, and the flight goes on: 0.2 s after the save nobody is hurt and
; nothing has landed or burst. At 0.6 s, two squares out, it is saved again -
; the save that can tell "the square it is over" from "the party's square" -
; and 2 s on it has flown out of reach and burst there, far off. `flooritems`
; says where the flask IS at each save (`at`, in squares) beside the square the
; game would write (`over`); loading each save finds the flask - whole - on the
; floor of the square its position was in.

