; --- A COSMETIC CLIP MOVES NO DICE (code-review C73) ----------------------------
; Which of a state's clips a monster plays draws from a stream of its own, never
; the combat RNG, so authoring one more clip cannot shift a seeded sweep's rolls.
; A skeleton swinging at the party (rungs/clips-skeleton.eval) swept over four
; seeds as the kind is authored - it ships one clip per state, so it draws
; nothing (TALLY `clipdraws=`) - and again with a second ATTACK clip (its walk,
; played as a swing: the test needs a clip the model ships, not a good look),
; which draws every time it starts a swing. Every other TALLY field must match,
; sample for sample. While the pick drew from the combat stream, each swing's
; draw shifted every roll after it. The table is put back at the end:
; `monsterclips` edits the live kind, which outlives a reset.

echo === clip-plain ===
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
goto eval_arena
monsterclips skeleton
sweep 4 rungs/clips-skeleton.eval

echo === clip-extra ===
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
goto eval_arena
monsterclips skeleton attack attack walk
sweep 4 rungs/clips-skeleton.eval
monsterclips skeleton attack attack

echo === end ===
